(* ==================================================================
   De-semantic Causal Topology — Formal Grammar
   Second Perspective Engine · Topology Layer (拓扑层)
   ------------------------------------------------------------------
   Version        : 2026.3  — EXTENSION to Language Standard 2026.2
   Notation       : ISO/IEC 14977 (Extended BNF)
   Normative ref  : 《SPL因果论 · 无语义拓扑语法规范》
   Related        : decision.ebnf (upper layer, .spd records)
   File extension : .tpg
   ------------------------------------------------------------------
   DECLARATION OF EXTENSION (语法扩展声明)
   This grammar does NOT replace decision.ebnf.  The two live on
   different layers and must not be mixed:

       .spd   upper layer  — Decision / Assumption / Dependency / Branch
                             describes, for humans, within which boundary
                             a decision holds.  Carries no execution
                             semantics (E301-E304 enforced by dsl.py).
       .tpg   topology     — □ / → / ⦿ plus relative labels △ / ◇.
                             The compile-level substrate the ten
                             operators act upon.  No semantics at all.

   Symbols introduced by this extension, beyond the五算子 already
   mapped in the normative reference:
       ⊙   origin anchor        (operator ORI)
       ⊞   topology construction (operator TPG)
       ⇄   reality feedback     (operator GRF)
       ↻   spiral superposition (orchestrator spiral)
       ⊛∞  evolution scan       (orchestrator evolve — proposals only)
       BFC binary fact check    (operator BFC — letter code, no new glyph;
                                 deliberately avoids a symbol so that the
                                 binary verdict never reads as a third value)
       META meta-causal ledger  (operator META — letter code, for the same
                                 reason: a ledger of measures must never be
                                 mistakable for an adjudication)

   CHANGE LOG
       2026.2  topological substrate: □/→/⦿, relative labels △/◇,
               operators ⊙ ORI · ⊞ TPG · ⇄ GRF · ↻ spiral · BFC
       2026.3  axiom 5 made load-bearing:
                 · edge parameter t — chain-internal time order
                 · process 4 of parallel checking — time order
                 · T305 fork · T307 inverted order · T308 unassignable
                 · meta-causal metrics A6 (narrative entropy) and
                   A10 (audit entropy) become reportable ledger fields
                 · evolution rules R-EVO-* (propose, never self-apply)

   DESIGN INVARIANT
   Symbols carry no semantics; semantics is produced by operators.
   No field in a .tpg record may express a conclusion, a
   recommendation, a ranking, a score, or an assigned probability.
   The labels △ / ◇ are RELATIVE and MUST NOT participate in
   adjudication — they exist for output mapping only.
   ================================================================== *)


(* ==================================================================
   1. DOCUMENT — top-level shape and block ordering
   ------------------------------------------------------------------
   Exactly one origin, at least one node, at least one edge,
   zero or more axioms.
   Block order is normative: Origin < Node < Edge < Axiom.
   Comment lines may appear anywhere.
   ================================================================== *)

topology        = { comment } , origin_block ,
                  { comment } , nodes_block ,
                  { comment } , edges_block ,
                  { comment } , [ axioms_block ] ,
                  { comment } ;

origin_block    = "Origin" , colon , text ;

nodes_block     = node , { { comment } , node } ;

edges_block     = edge , { { comment } , edge } ;

axioms_block    = axiom , { { comment } , axiom } ;


(* ==================================================================
   2. CORE PRODUCTIONS
   ------------------------------------------------------------------
   origin  — the first origin event: the chain has no beginning
             without it; every later node owes its order to it.
   node    — □ an entity node.  No intrinsic attribute whatsoever.
             Delete every incident edge and the node disappears.
   edge    — → a causal directed edge with optional constraint
             parameters.  Direction determines the relative labels.
   axiom   — ⦿ a global constraint.  Immutable, globally in force.
   ================================================================== *)

node            = "Node" , space , id , [ colon , text ] ;

edge            = "Edge" , colon , space , id , space , arrow , space , id ,
                  [ params ] ;

axiom           = "Axiom" , space , id , colon , kind , [ params ] ;

params          = space , "[" , param , { comma , param } , "]" ;

param           = ( "w" | "weight" )     , eq , number
                | ( "v" | "validity" )   , eq , text
                | ( "f" | "falsifiable" ), eq , boolean
                | ( "d" | "delta" )      , eq , text
                | ( "t" | "time" )       , eq , integer ;

(* --- t : chain-internal time order (axiom 5) -----------------------
   Optional.  Absent means "not declared", and the engine then derives
   the order by longest path — a pure function of the structure, so
   omitting t never changes a topology fingerprint.

   When declared it MUST satisfy   t(src) <= t < t(dst)  :
   a preceding cause precedes its succeeding effect.  A declared value
   violating this range is T307 (order inverted).

   t is a cardinal, never a timestamp: the grammar has no clock.
   Time here is "the order of a chain", not "a moment in the world". *)
integer         = [ "-" ] , digit , { digit } ;


(* ==================================================================
   3. LEXICAL ELEMENTS
   ================================================================== *)

(* --- direction: ASCII and the normative Unicode arrow are equal --- *)

arrow           = "->" | "→" ;

(* --- axiom kinds: only three are admitted at this version ------- *)
(*     weight_range      [lo=0.0, hi=1.0]                           *)
(*     max_out_degree    [max=4]                                   *)
(*     required_param    [param=weight]                            *)

kind            = "weight_range" | "max_out_degree" | "required_param" ;

boolean         = "true" | "false" ;

number          = [ "-" ] , digit , { digit } , [ "." , digit , { digit } ] ;

id              = letter , { letter | digit | "_" } ;

text            = { space } , nonspace , { graphic | space } ;

comment         = "#" , { graphic | space } ;

colon           = ":" | "：" ;
comma           = "," ;
eq              = "=" ;
space           = " " ;
letter          = upper | lower ;
upper           = ? U+0041 .. U+005A , i.e. "A" to "Z" ? ;
lower           = ? U+0061 .. U+007A , i.e. "a" to "z" ? ;
digit           = ? U+0030 .. U+0039 , i.e. "0" to "9" ? ;
nonspace        = ? any Unicode character except U+0009, U+000A, U+000D, U+0020 ? ;
graphic         = ? any Unicode character except U+0009, U+000A, U+000D ? ;
newline         = ? U+000A | U+000D U+000A ? ;


(* ==================================================================
   4. RELATIVE LABELS (advisory surface only, never adjudicated)
   ------------------------------------------------------------------
   Theorem of relative labels:
     1. A node that is ◇ on the chain A→B is △ on the chain B→C.
        No node owns a label.
     2. A c↔d double-constraint edge is legal: c and d are each
        other's assumption and output.
     3. Labels are stripped before any structural computation;
        removing them changes no result.
   ================================================================== *)

upstream_label   = "△" | "@in" ;
downstream_label = "◇" | "@out" ;


(* ==================================================================
   5. CONDITIONAL / SEMANTIC RULES
   ------------------------------------------------------------------
   Not expressible in pure EBNF and therefore enforced by the
   topology validator (inlined in Second Perspective Engine.py,
   Zone ② — TopologyValidator).  Normative, not
   advisory.  Severity follows the normative reference:
   consistency / constraint checks are FATAL (halt the derivation,
   produce no result); closure and time-order checks are WARNINGS
   (may be forced through, but the result is void).

   The four processes run in parallel, with no serial waiting.
   Time order is a process of its own rather than part of closure,
   because they ask different questions and may fail independently:
      closure      is the graph self-consistent
      time order   is this graph still *a chain*

   -- process 1 · consistency (FATAL) --
   T101  node identities MUST be globally unique, and no (src,dst)
         pair MAY carry two mutually contradictory relations
   T102  duplicate edges with the same (src,dst,relation) MUST
         carry identical parameters
   -- process 2 · constraint satisfaction (FATAL) --
   T201  every edge weight MUST lie inside the ⦿ weight_range
   T202  every parameter declared required by ⦿ MUST be present
   T203  out-degree MUST NOT exceed the ⦿ max_out_degree
   -- process 3 · closure (WARNING, result void) --
   T301  every edge endpoint MUST be a declared node
   T302  every declared node SHOULD be touched by at least one edge
   T303  the directed graph MUST be acyclic — a cycle A→B→C→¬A is
         a causal paradox, for time order is absolute and chains
         cannot fold back onto themselves
   -- layer rule (operator level, not grammar level) --
   R-ORIGIN  the origin MUST NOT drift across spiral layers
   R-STACK   the frozen subgraph MUST grow monotonically: a node
             declared converged may not vanish in a later layer
   -- binary fact check (operator level, not grammar level) --
   R-FACT-1  every fact under check MUST carry both a claim and evidence;
             an evidence vacuum halts the derivation
   R-FACT-2  mutually negating evidence on one claim halts the derivation;
             the layer does not pick a side
   R-FACT-3  a claim already verified false MUST NOT remain in the
             assumption set
   R-FACT-4  the layer admits true or false ONLY.  A claim whose truth
             value is not declared yields a status (VERDICT_UNDECLARED),
             never a third truth value — "unknown" is not an answer
   -- process 4 · time order (WARNING, result void; axiom 5) --
   T305  one (src,dst) pair MUST NOT be declared more than once.
         "Parallel" is several chains each ordered on its own;
         "branch" is one chain splitting its future, and SPL is
         strongly deterministic — it admits the former only
   T307  a declared t MUST lie in [ t(src), t(dst) - 1 ] :
         a preceding cause precedes its succeeding effect
   T308  a monotone assignment MUST exist.  A directed cycle leaves
         the order unassignable, and without order there is no chain
   NOTE  multiple roots are LEGAL — that IS "parallel".  Only a
         repeated (src,dst) pair is a violation, never a wide fan-out.
   -- meta-causal ledger (operator META · T2 — never blocking) --
   A6    narrative entropy = masked characters / total characters.
         A rational number, never a probability.  It measures the
         degree of occlusion, nothing else: 「随机」不在混沌之中，
         只在观测者的知识缺口之中 — attributing an unresolved
         antecedent to chance is the error this metric exposes
   A10   audit entropy = provenance entries per layer, the discrete
         form of d(version)/dt.  A bounded A10 is the arithmetic
         precondition for evolution to converge to S* (天道)
   R-META-1  META MUST NOT block.  A measure is not a missing input,
             and only missing inputs halt a derivation (I-1 非猜测)
   -- evolution (orchestrator evolve · never self-applying) --
   R-EVO-1  evolve() MAY emit proposals; it MUST NOT apply them.
            Three identities, invariantly:
                applies_automatically = false
                requires_human         = true
                auto_applied           = 0
   R-EVO-2  any change to the operator set requires an explicit,
            named human approval.  That approval is RECORDED, and the
            engine's adjudication rules are NOT modified by it:
            applied_to_code = false, requires_code_change = true
   R-EVO-3  the lineage (generation · operator-set hash · pipeline
            order) MUST be carried by the report and the chain, so
            that an older generation's chain root stays recomputable.
            This is precisely why evolution and reproducibility can
            coexist instead of excluding each other
   R-EVO-4  halting is the minimal fixed point g_{n+1} == g_n
            (graph isomorphism), not "the budget ran out"
   ================================================================== *)


(* ==================================================================
   6. WORKED EXAMPLE — .tpg
   ------------------------------------------------------------------
Origin: 2026Q1 试点立项

Node: n0
Node: nD
Node: nQ
Node: nA1
Node: nA2

Edge: n0 -> nD [w=1.0]
Edge: nD -> nQ [w=1.0 t=1]
Edge: nA1 -> nD [f=false]
Edge: nA2 -> nD [f=false]

Axiom: w1: weight_range [lo=0.0, hi=1.0]
Axiom: d1: max_out_degree [max=4]

   (Validated output: ✅ consistency · ✅ constraint · ✅ closure
    · ✅ time_order.
    Derived order by longest path: n0=0, nA1=0, nA2=0, nD=1, nQ=2.
    Roots {n0, nA1, nA2} = three chains running in parallel — legal.
    Writing n0 -> nD twice would emit T305 (fork).
    Writing n0 -> nD -> n0 would emit T303 and leave the order
    unassignable (T308); the same graph written nA1 → nD → n0 as a
    cycle would do the same.)
   ================================================================== *)

(* ==================================================================
   END OF GRAMMAR — Topology Layer 2026.3
   ================================================================== *)
